# turbo-bible — the K-popup "fetch cross-references" affordance.
#
# Render with:
#   just xrefs-screenshot            # or: vhs demo/xrefs-fetch.tape
#
# Standalone (not part of the 21-shot screenshots.tour, like word-diff.tape /
# og-image.tape) so re-rendering this feature's capture never churns the rest
# of the set. Emits:
#   docs/screenshots/24-xrefs-fetch.png   (the affordance — the feature)
#
# Unlike the rest of the set this clears XDG_DATA_HOME too (not just
# XDG_CONFIG_HOME): a fresh data dir means only the embedded en-kjv extracts and
# xrefs.db is the install-time empty stand-in, so Db::has_xrefs() is false and
# the K-popup is in its missing-data state — exactly what a fresh cargo/brew
# install sees. (The screenshots.tour uses the dev's real, populated xrefs.db,
# which would never show the affordance.)
#
# The companion docs/screenshots/25-xrefs-fetch-before.png is the pre-feature
# `main` behaviour (the dead-end "(no notes or cross-references on this verse)"
# popup on the same verse) — a pinned baseline for the before/after pair. It is
# NOT regenerated by this tape: the affordance replaced that state, so the old
# behaviour can't be reproduced from this tree.

Output demo/_xrefs-fetch-trace.gif

Set Shell        "bash"
Set Width        1600
Set Height       860
Set FontSize     19
Set Padding      18
Set Theme        "Catppuccin Mocha"
Set TypingSpeed  20ms

# --- Setup (hidden): fresh XDG (empty xrefs stand-in) + pinned daily verse ---
Hide
Type "export XDG_CONFIG_HOME=$(mktemp -d)"
Enter
Type "export XDG_DATA_HOME=$(mktemp -d)"
Enter
Type "export SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1717000000"
Enter
Type "export TB_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Type "./target/release/turbo-bible --translation en-kjv --book JHN --chapter 3"
Enter
Show
Sleep 3500ms

# Land on John 3:16 — which carries 27 cross-references, so the empty stand-in
# is conspicuous — and the popup title reads a recognisable verse.
Type ":"
Sleep 200ms
Type "John 3:16"
Sleep 400ms
Enter
Sleep 1200ms

# K opens the notes / cross-reference popup → the fetch affordance, because the
# dataset isn't installed in this fresh data dir.
Type "K"
Sleep 1200ms
Screenshot "docs/screenshots/24-xrefs-fetch.png"
Sleep 400ms

# --- Quit ---------------------------------------------------------------
Hide
Type "q"
Sleep 400ms
